00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.910 align:start position:0%
 
this is dave klein reading for mark  delaney i've never envied the  development cycle that comes with  working on an annual sports game series  when you consider how much time and  money goes into any other big budget  project asking a studio to constantly  churn out a game that is both functional  and consistent but also fresh and  exciting every single year seems unfair  nba 2k 23 is incredibly impressive  regardless but even more so in light of  this tight dev cycle with a deep suite  of fun game modes improved encore  gameplay and a deeper social experience  it feels like the team of visual  concepts managed to freeze time and  spend longer than the typical cycle on  this exceptional nba sim  [Music]  it's hard to know where to begin with  nba 2k 23 because in ways both big and  small there's a lot of new stuff to see  for me though it starts with the jordan  challenge for the first time since nba  2k11 you can relive highlights from the  career of the greatest player in nba  history more than just a rehash of a  mode absent for over a decade this  renewed jordan challenge is like a  modern remake of that original concept  beginning in his college career at north  carolina you'll play through 15 of  jordan's biggest games and work to  recreate stat lines and other outcomes  like a time traveler seeking to relive  jordan's forever on replay highlights  conceptually this is as it was before  albeit now with 5 more games than the  original iteration but the finer details  are where the jordan challenge really  shines in 2k 23 era appropriate filters  retro on-screen graphics and even long  gun arenas and fittingly depressed  spectators work together to transport  players to the time and place of each  game spanning the 80s and 90s  before each game the visual concepts  team includes new interview segments  with players commentators coaches and  others who witnessed the greatness of  michael jordan first hand collectively  it gives the whole mode the feeling of  an interactive museum to unrivaled  basketball achievements and playing it  has been the first time in my life that  a sports game gave me goosebumps  not content to only have jordan reside  on the game's figurative memory lane my  nba mode is also infused with many of  these same features including even  throwback teams like the seattle  supersonics these features wouldn't make  sense in a modern setting and so the  game allows you to start your league in  one of three bygone eras across the 80s  90s and 2000s this allows you to  position your team to draft or trade for  the contemporary or incoming stars of  each era and recreate basketball history  from the starting point like creating  alternate realities where lebron james  was drafted by philly or jordan never  retired for two years in the middle of  his prime  the league will change as you go too  with rule books getting updated dominant  play styles changing over the years and  teams relocating or not if you decide  your nba alt universe keeps the sonics  where they belong for example  these two modes represent ways this  year's game feels like it goes above and  beyond other sports sims just aren't  offering this type of content for their  players it's a remarkable thing and  feels handled with care and attention  from a studio that must be full of real  basketball fanatics the love of the game  is pouring out of these two modes and  would merely by themselves qualify nba  2k 23 as a must play for basketball fans  nba 2k has long been a series that  sweats the small stuff too wildly  lifelike player animations best in class  commentary and unmatched broadcast style  presentation all return with impressive  added touches like different commentary  teams depending on which mode you're  playing nba nba2k has a long put some  other sports series  which i won't name but you can probably  guess to shame with such attention to  detail and these little things have an  outsized effect in the end making the  series the most enjoyable sports game  every single year  though the nba itself generally favors  the three ball in real life that's not  the case for all players of course but  last year's game made sharpshooters out  of anyone with an open look it was  unrealistic and altered what is arguably  the most important aspect online pickup  games with friends and rivals 2k 23  focuses largely on giving power back to  the strong finishers and slashers of the  league preventing back-to-back years  where everyone looks like steph curry  modeled after the play of buxford  giannis hadn't compo this year's game  feels better balanced right away for  different play styles those who aren't  natural shooters have regressed to  something more realistic while those who  lean into the paint and bully defenders  now feel just as dominant as a shooter  from behind the arc in turn this has  made online pvp games more enjoyable as  they no longer feel like three-point  contests for many players the heart of  the game is always my player though the  actual narrative of each year's game  varies in quality i found this year's  story to be surprisingly enjoyable in it  you'll land with the team of your  choosing as the 18th overall pick and  nba draft but selected right after you  is shep owens your college rival and the  player your team's fans actually wanted  through months of hard work on the court  and some silly pr campaigns in the city  your job is to win over hearts and minds  sports game story modes like sports  movies can get corny in a hurry but this  year's story manages to defy odds and  land on the right side of the tracks  with its constant attempts at humor i  usually wasn't cringing and was  sometimes even laughing which adds up to  the story better than most in others in  this space perhaps the best part of my  career is how well it integrates right  into the city as the mmo-like live  service hub of the game the city is  where players spend the most hours after  they finish the story knowing that the  team has designed this year's game to  give you narrative reasons for running  around the city completing quests for  dozens of npcs like as an rpg you'll be  winning over districts of fans like a  san andreas turf war but here your  weapons will be charity work endorsement  deals and the occasional viral tweet  after years of the city and its  predecessor of the neighborhood then  mode still feels like an accomplishment  like the jordan challenge and my nba  eras this social hub is something only  nba 2k is doing and helps separate it  from the rest of the pack making it easy  for fans of multiple sports games to  know where to invest their time with  tons of modes and attractions including  a new theater where limited time modes  now reside on a rotating schedule the  city isn't perfect though for those who  don't want to run from quest to court  and vice versa skateboards and bikes are  back but they control so poorly and  always have that i'm more likely to stay  on foot and accept the speed decrease  thankfully now fast travel points have  been added in the form of subway  stations and this year's city is  actually about 30 percent smaller due to  fan demand for a more dense cityscape  still both quest and travel distances  will sometimes call for using  skateboards but they're frustratingly  unwieldy  if you're not new to the series you'll  likely already know how invasive the  microtransactions  mtx are even at its past heights the pay  model has been the thing taking this  series down a peg or two and it's still  an issue here the problem is twofold on  one hand the game's my team mode is just  as bad as any comparable mode such as  ultimate team in ea sports games it's  pay to win without a doubt given how any  player can simply buy up unlimited card  packs until they've landed a dominant  team but the game's mtx continues to  dampen the city too as this same virtual  currency that can upgrade your squad in  my team can also dramatically improve  your my player protagonist too  as that player eventually migrates out  of the story and into the city it causes  a my team-like rift between those who  grind for greatness and those who paid  their way up the ranks it's clear some  percentage of the players may prefer the  game lets them upgrade right away but  then they have to face them in the  city's courts and other pvp modes feels  like getting stuck in a first person  shooter lobby with wall hackers and  aimbotters making it so the same  currency buys tattoos repaints  skateboards and upgrades or player feels  like a long broken feature that the game  just keeps returning to each september  the city is also smothered by product  placement in a way that is so over the  top it would be hilarious if it wasn't  giving me such a dark preview of the  so-called metaverse virtually everything  is a commercial from gatorade and nike  to mobile and nokia it feels like i  can't even high-five a teammate without  it being brought to me by mountain dew  these issues do hinder nba 2k 23 from  being historically great but all else  adds up to what is still an exceptional  basketball game made with an intense  attention to detail and a love of the  game on the court nba 2k 23 looks and  feels lifelike and exciting in every  drive and the new and revamped modes  treat the nba like a revered historical  monument in those important ways it does  its best to reflect jordan's greatness  and shows both nba newcomers and  historians what it's like to play like  mike  [Music]  supposedly jordan wasn't a three-point  shooter how about six in the first half  [Music]  brutal wow

